The present petition has been preferred for the following relief/s:
(i) for issuance of an appropriate order or direction quashing and setting aside the Order dated 15.11.2024 passed by the District Land Acquisition Officer, Patna in LA Case No. 23/2022-23 (Annexure-P/14) whereby compensation for the remaining portion of the Petitioner's acquired land has been withheld on the basis of a third-party Patna High Court CWJC No.1610 of 2026(2) dt.02-02-2026 objection;
(ii) that the present writ application is being filed in the nature of Mandamus,
commanding the respondent authorities, particularly the District Land Acquisition Officer, Patna, to release the withheld compensation amount for approximately 3 decimals of land (part of 23 decimals acquired) belonging to the petitioner situated at Mauja Rukanpura, District Patna, acquired for the Patna Metro Rukanpura Station Project, along with interest and statutory benefits under the Right to Fair Compensation and Transparency in Land Acquisition, Rehabilitation and Resettlement Act, 2013 (RFCTLARR Act, 2013);
Parshuram Singh vs The State Of Bihar on 2 February, 2026 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/137670327/
1 (iii) that the present writ petition is being filed in the nature of Mandamies for Issuance of an appropriate order or direction declaring that the action of the District Land Acquisition Officer, Patna, in Patna High Court CWJC No.1610 of 2026(2)
dt.02-02-2026 withholding compensation for approximately 3 decimals of land, despite the Petitioner's name being recorded in the acquisition notification and the award, is illegal, arbitrary and without jurisdiction;
(iv) that the present writ petition is being filed in the nature of Mandamus for commanding the Respondent Authorities to forthwith conduct a fresh and lawful remeasurement of the Petitioner's acquired land in his presence and in accordance with law and further to demarcate two decimals of land and hand over same to the Petitioner;
(v) that the present writ petition is being filed in the nature of Mandamus for a direction declaring that the District Land Acquisition Officer has no authority under Right to Fair Compensation and Transparency in Land Acquisition, Rehabilitation and Resettlement Act, 2013 to adjudicate title disputes or to withhold Patna High Court CWJC No.1610 of 2026(2) dt.02-02-2026 compensation payable under a validly prepared award;
(vi) and pass any such order/orders which this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and proper.
3. Let the parties file their respective responses in next six weeks.
4. Issue notice to respondent no.07 both by registered cover with A/D as well as ordinary process for which requisites etc. must be filed within two weeks from today failing which this application shall stand rejected without further reference to a Bench.
5.
